# Documentation Update Reminder

When modifying files in the `packages/` directory:

## For New Features

If you are adding a new feature, API method, configuration option, or loading strategy:

1. **Add a TODO comment** in the code pointing to the documentation need:
   ```js
   // TODO: Document in docs/index.html - [brief description]
   ```

2. **Create a TODO task** for the documentation update:
   - Feature name and what it does
   - Which section of docs/index.html it belongs in
   - Any code examples needed
   - Whether screenshots/recordings are required

## Documentation Sections Reference

The docs are structured as follows in `docs/index.html`:

- **Quick Start** - Installation and basic setup
- **Loading Strategies** - eager, visible, event modifiers
- **Slots** - Default and named slot usage
- **Loading States** - The .loading.html feature
- **Vite Plugin** - Plugin configuration options
- **API Reference** - Full method/option documentation

## Checklist for New Features

- [ ] Add inline code comments explaining the feature
- [ ] Update relevant README.md in the package
- [ ] Add documentation TODO for docs/index.html
- [ ] Consider if demo/example is needed
- [ ] Note if screenshot/recording placeholder is required

## Example TODO Format

When adding a new loading strategy called "idle":

```js
// TODO: Document 'idle' strategy in docs/index.html#loading-strategies
// - Uses requestIdleCallback to load during browser idle time
// - Usage: x-component.idle="modal"
// - Needs demo recording showing load timing
```
